# Island Dash asset manifest: logical name -> model file, normalization, material overrides.
# Swapping an art pack = editing this file. Gameplay code only uses the logical names.
#
#   name              path (relative to assets/, or "cube")              scale        pivot          [tint=r,g,b] [emissive=r,g,b,strength] [roughness=x]
#
# scale : one number or x,y,z; brings the model to the kit unit size listed in the comment.
# pivot : x,y,z in model units, added before scaling, so the model's base sits on the piece origin.
#         Kenney models are already bottom-centered (0,0,0). A "cube" primitive is centered, so it needs 0,0.5,0.
# Missing names (or files that fail to load) render as placeholder cubes instead of stopping the game.

# --- Characters (kit height ~1.3 m) — Platformer Kit ---
player            models/kenney_platformer/character-ooli.glb         1.45         0,0,0          tint=0.86,0.88,0.92
enemy_patrol      models/kenney_platformer/character-oodi.glb         1.35         0,0,0
enemy_chase       models/kenney_platformer/character-oozi.glb         1.4          0,0,0          tint=1,0.55,0.55

# --- Pickups — Platformer Kit ---
crystal           models/kenney_platformer/jewel.glb                  1.6          0,0,0          emissive=0.1,0.3,1,0.9 roughness=0.25
heart             models/kenney_platformer/heart.glb                  1.8          0,0,0          emissive=1,0.15,0.2,0.6
checkpoint_flag   models/kenney_platformer/flag.glb                   1.1          0,0,0

